{"name": "RAG - Extract Text.step", "displayName": "RAG - Extract Text.step", "localDisplayName": "RAG - Extract Text.step", "description": "Extracts text elements from every new or changed document in the RAG inventory through the rag_core extractor registry; corrupt documents are marked failed without failing the flow.", "localDescription": "Extracts text elements from every new or changed document in the RAG inventory through the rag_core extractor registry; corrupt documents are marked failed without failing the flow.", "properties": {}, "metadataVersion": 0.0, "version": 2, "type": "code", "flowMetadata": {"inputPorts": [{"name": "_rgex_inventory", "displayName": "_rgex_inventory", "localDisplayName": "_rgex_inventory", "minEntries": 0, "maxEntries": 1, "defaultEntries": 0, "type": "table"}], "outputPorts": [{"name": "_rgex_elements", "displayName": "_rgex_elements", "localDisplayName": "_rgex_elements", "minEntries": 0, "maxEntries": 1, "defaultEntries": 0, "type": "table"}, {"name": "_rgex_invout", "displayName": "_rgex_invout", "localDisplayName": "_rgex_invout", "minEntries": 0, "maxEntries": 1, "defaultEntries": 0, "type": "table"}]}, "ui": "{\n\t\"showPageContentOnly\": true,\n\t\"pages\": [\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t\"id\": \"pageDefinition\",\n\t\t\t\"type\": \"page\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"Definition\",\n\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgex_info\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Extracts text elements from every new or changed document in the inventory. Formats: plaintext, markdown, CSV/JSON, HTML and the PDF text layer (pypdfium2); markitdown formats when that package is installed. A corrupt document is marked failed and skipped - the flow keeps running.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgex_inventory\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"inputtable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Document inventory (from RAG - List Documents):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgex_extractor\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Force a specific extractor (blank = choose by file format):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgex_sectionAdvanced\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Runtime\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgex_ragCorePath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"textfield\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SAS Content folder holding rag_core:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgex_elements\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"outputtable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Extracted elements output:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgex_invout\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"outputtable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Updated inventory output (wire this one forward):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t]\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t\"id\": \"pageAbout\",\n\t\t\t\"type\": \"page\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"About\",\n\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textAbout\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"RAG - Extract Text step\\n==========\\n\\nRe-reads the bytes of every new or changed document and runs the rag_core extractor registry. Oversized texts are split at paragraph boundaries so they fit table columns; the chunker re-joins them. Documents whose extraction fails are marked failed in the updated inventory - they retry on the next run.\\n\\nFlow wiring: RAG - List Documents \u2192 RAG - Extract Text (inventory) \u2192 RAG - Chunk Documents (elements + updated inventory) \u2192 RAG - Embed Chunks (chunks) \u2192 RAG - Load Vector Store (embedded chunks + updated inventory). Always pass each step's UPDATED inventory forward so per-document failures and chunk counts reach the ledger.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionPrereqs\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Pre-requisites\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textPrereqs\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Tested on SAS Viya 2026 (Stable).\\n\\n* The rag_core runtime must be deployed to SAS Content (default: /SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core) with deploy-rag-content.ps1/.sh - keep that folder read-only for regular users.\\n* The compute context's Python needs the requests package.\\n* pypdfium2 for the PDF text layer, markitdown for Office formats (each optional - matching extractors deactivate when a package is missing).\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionChangelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Changelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textChangelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"* Version: 1.0 (28JUL2026)\\n      - Initial version\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t]\n\t\t}\n\t],\n\t\"syntaxversion\": \"1.3.0\",\n\t\"values\": {\n\t\t\"_rgex_extractor\": \"\",\n\t\t\"_rgex_ragCorePath\": \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core\"\n\t}\n}", "templates": {"SAS": "/******************************************************************************\n * Copyright \u00a9 2026, SAS Institute Inc., Cary, NC, USA.  All Rights Reserved.\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n *\n * RAG - Extract Text: re-read every new/changed document from the inventory\n * and extract text elements through the rag_core extractor registry. A\n * corrupt document is marked failed in the inventory and never fails the\n * flow (per-document failure contract, design section 2).\n * Thin shell over rag_core.steps.run_extract - see the About tab.\n ******************************************************************************/\n%macro _rgex_setup;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgex_elements) %then %global _rgex_elements;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgex_elements)) EQ 0 %then %let _rgex_elements = WORK.RAG_ELEMENTS;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgex_invout) %then %global _rgex_invout;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgex_invout)) EQ 0 %then %let _rgex_invout = WORK.RAG_INVENTORY_EXTRACTED;\n%mend _rgex_setup;\n%_rgex_setup;\n\n%let _rgex_viyaHost = %sysfunc(getoption(SERVICESBASEURL));\n%let _rgex_rc = 1;\n%let _rgex_error = The Python program did not run.;\n%let _rgex_summary = ;\n%let _rgex_nel = 0;\n%let _rgex_ninv = 0;\n\n%macro _rgex_export(portvar, file);\n    %if %symexist(&portvar.) %then %do;\n        %if %length(%superq(&&portvar.)) GT 0 %then %do;\n            %if %sysfunc(exist(&&&portvar..)) %then %do;\n                filename _rgex_io \"%sysfunc(pathname(work))/&file.\";\n                proc json out=_rgex_io noSASTags;\n                    export &&&portvar..;\n                run; quit;\n                filename _rgex_io clear;\n            %end;\n        %end;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgex_export;\n%_rgex_export(_rgex_inventory, rgex_inventory_in.json);\n\nproc python restart;\nsubmit;\ndef main():\n    import json\n    import os\n    import sys\n    import tempfile\n    import time\n    import traceback\n\n    def sas_safe(text):\n        \"\"\"Strings crossing into SAS.logMessage/SAS.symput are embedded into\n        generated SAS statements - quotes and macro characters corrupt the\n        code stream (verified live). EVERY such string goes through here.\"\"\"\n        cleaned = str(text)\n        for ch in (\"'\", '\"', \"%\", \"&\", \";\"):\n            cleaned = cleaned.replace(ch, \" \")\n        return cleaned\n\n    def M(msg):\n        SAS.logMessage(\"RAGEXTRACT \" + sas_safe(msg))\n\n    try:\n        import requests\n    except Exception:\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgex_error\", \"The Python environment of this compute \"\n                                   \"context lacks the requests package - see \"\n                                   \"the RAG administration guide.\")\n        return\n\n    BASE = str(SAS.symget(\"_rgex_viyaHost\") or \"\").rstrip(\"/\")\n    TOKEN = os.environ.get(\"SAS_SERVICES_TOKEN\", \"\")\n    AUTH = {\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + TOKEN}\n    VERIFY = os.environ.get(\"SSLCALISTLOC\") or os.environ.get(\"CAS_CLIENT_SSL_CA_LIST\") or True\n    WORKPATH = SAS.workpath if SAS.workpath.endswith(os.sep) else SAS.workpath + os.sep\n\n    P = {name: str(SAS.symget(name) or \"\").strip() for name in [\n        \"_rgex_extractor\",\n        \"_rgex_ragCorePath\",\n    ]}\n\n    def read_rows(filename, missing_message):\n        path = WORKPATH + filename\n        if not os.path.exists(path):\n            raise RuntimeError(missing_message)\n        with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            data = json.load(fh)\n        rows = []\n        for row in data if isinstance(data, list) else []:\n            rows.append({str(k).lower(): v for k, v in row.items()})\n        return rows\n\n    def write_rows(filename, rows, columns, numeric=()):\n        out = []\n        for row in rows:\n            rec = {}\n            for column in columns:\n                value = row.get(column)\n                if column in numeric:\n                    try:\n                        rec[column] = float(value or 0)\n                    except Exception:\n                        rec[column] = 0.0\n                else:\n                    rec[column] = \"\" if value is None else str(value)\n            out.append(rec)\n        with open(WORKPATH + filename, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            json.dump(out, fh)\n        return len(out)\n\n    try:\n        # ---- rag_core bootstrap: download the governed SAS Content folder --\n        def get_json(endpoint, **params):\n            response = requests.get(BASE + endpoint, params=params, headers=AUTH,\n                                    verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 30))\n            response.raise_for_status()\n            return response.json()\n\n        def download_folder(folder_id, local_dir):\n            os.makedirs(local_dir, exist_ok=True)\n            count = 0\n            members = get_json(f\"/folders/folders/{folder_id}/members\", limit=200)\n            for member in members.get(\"items\", []):\n                uri = member.get(\"uri\", \"\")\n                if \"/files/files/\" in uri:\n                    content = requests.get(BASE + uri + \"/content\", headers=AUTH,\n                                           verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 60))\n                    content.raise_for_status()\n                    with open(os.path.join(local_dir, member[\"name\"]), \"wb\") as fh:\n                        fh.write(content.content)\n                    count += 1\n                elif \"/folders/folders/\" in uri:\n                    count += download_folder(uri.rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1],\n                                             os.path.join(local_dir, member[\"name\"]))\n            return count\n\n        core_path = P[\"_rgex_ragCorePath\"] or \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core\"\n        root = requests.get(BASE + \"/folders/folders/@item\",\n                            params={\"path\": core_path}, headers=AUTH,\n                            verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 30))\n        if root.status_code != 200:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"rag_core folder {core_path} not found \"\n                               f\"(HTTP {root.status_code}) - deploy it per the \"\n                               \"administration guide\")\n        staging = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"rag_core_\")\n        n_files = download_folder(root.json()[\"id\"], os.path.join(staging, \"rag_core\"))\n        sys.path.insert(0, staging)\n        import rag_core\n        M(f\"rag_core {rag_core.RAG_CORE_VERSION} bootstrapped ({n_files} files)\")\n\n        from rag_core.extractors import ExtractorRegistry\n        from rag_core.steps import ELEMENT_COLUMNS, LEDGER_COLUMNS, run_extract\n\n        inventory_columns = LEDGER_COLUMNS + [\"extractor\"]\n        inventory = read_rows(\"rgex_inventory_in.json\",\n                              \"the inventory input port is not connected - \"\n                              \"wire the RAG - List Documents output into \"\n                              \"this step\")\n        registry = ExtractorRegistry()\n        unavailable = registry.catalog()[\"unavailable\"]\n        if unavailable:\n            M(f\"extractors unavailable (packages missing): {unavailable}\")\n\n        elements, updated = run_extract(inventory, registry,\n                                        extractor_name=P[\"_rgex_extractor\"] or None,\n                                        log=M)\n        n_elements = write_rows(\"rgex_elements_out.json\", elements,\n                                ELEMENT_COLUMNS, numeric=(\"level\", \"page\"))\n        n_inventory = write_rows(\"rgex_inventory_out.json\", updated,\n                                 inventory_columns, numeric=(\"chunk_count\",))\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgex_nel\", str(n_elements))\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgex_ninv\", str(n_inventory))\n        n_docs = sum(1 for r in updated\n                     if r.get(\"extractor\") and r.get(\"status\") != \"failed\")\n        n_failed = sum(1 for r in updated if r.get(\"status\") == \"failed\")\n        summary = (f\"{n_elements} elements from {n_docs} documents, \"\n                   f\"{n_failed} failed\")\n        M(summary)\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgex_summary\", sas_safe(summary)[:400])\n\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgex_rc\", \"0\")\n    except Exception as error:\n        error_text = f\"{type(error).__name__}: {error}\"\n        M(\"failed: \" + sas_safe(error_text))\n        print(traceback.format_exc())\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgex_error\", sas_safe(error_text)[:500])\n\n\nmain()\nendsubmit;\nrun; quit;\nproc python terminate;\nrun; quit;\n\n%macro _rgex_emit_elements;\n    %if &_rgex_rc. NE 0 %then %return;\n    %if &_rgex_nel. GT 0 %then %do;\n        filename rgexelo \"%sysfunc(pathname(work))/rgex_elements_out.json\";\n        libname rgexelj json fileref=rgexelo;\n        data &_rgex_elements.(compress=yes);\n            length doc_id $ 40 type $ 16 text $ 32000 level 8 page 8\n                   heading_path $ 1024;\n            set rgexelj.root(drop=ordinal_root);\n        run;\n        libname rgexelj clear;\n        filename rgexelo clear;\n    %end;\n    %else %do;\n        data &_rgex_elements.(compress=yes);\n            length doc_id $ 40 type $ 16 text $ 32000 level 8 page 8\n                   heading_path $ 1024;\n            call missing(of _all_);\n            stop;\n        run;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgex_emit_elements;\n%_rgex_emit_elements;\n\n%macro _rgex_emit_inventory;\n    %if &_rgex_rc. NE 0 %then %return;\n    %if &_rgex_ninv. GT 0 %then %do;\n        filename rgexino \"%sysfunc(pathname(work))/rgex_inventory_out.json\";\n        libname rgexinj json fileref=rgexino;\n        data &_rgex_invout.(compress=yes);\n            length doc_id $ 40 source_uri $ 1024 source_kind $ 16\n                   content_hash $ 64 mtime $ 32 status $ 12 error_text $ 512\n                   pipeline_version $ 32 config_hash $ 32 chunk_count 8\n                   run_id $ 32 updated_at $ 24 extractor $ 64;\n            set rgexinj.root(drop=ordinal_root);\n        run;\n        libname rgexinj clear;\n        filename rgexino clear;\n    %end;\n    %else %do;\n        data &_rgex_invout.(compress=yes);\n            length doc_id $ 40 source_uri $ 1024 source_kind $ 16\n                   content_hash $ 64 mtime $ 32 status $ 12 error_text $ 512\n                   pipeline_version $ 32 config_hash $ 32 chunk_count 8\n                   run_id $ 32 updated_at $ 24 extractor $ 64;\n            call missing(of _all_);\n            stop;\n        run;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgex_emit_inventory;\n%_rgex_emit_inventory;\n\ndata _null_;\n    if \"&_rgex_rc.\" ne \"0\" then do;\n        putLog \"ERROR: RAG - Extract Text failed: %superq(_rgex_error)\";\n        abort 42;\n    end;\n    putLog \"NOTE: RAG - Extract Text: %superq(_rgex_summary)\";\nrun;"}}